sis to move into the repair phase.","command":{"name":"express_hypothesis","args":{"hypothesis":"The crun-13 bug is caused by the container process launch using `execvp(def->process->args[0], def->process->args)` in `src/libcrun/container.c`. When `args[0]` is a bare command such as `sh`, `execvp` searches `$PATH` from the runtime process environment rather than reliably using the OCI `process.env` PATH inside the container. Thus PATH lookup can happen with the wrong environment and fail or execute inconsistently. The fix should make container process execution resolve bare argv[0] using the OCI-configured PATH after container setup, or install/use the OCI environment for exec, then exec the resolved container executable instead of relying on host/runtime PATH lookup."}}}{"thoughts":"With the root cause localized to container process exec, the next focused step is to inspect nearby symbols in `src/libcrun/container.c` so I can identify where the OCI process environment is applied before line 652 and design the smallest safe fix for PATH lookup without disturbing hook execution or utility `execvp` calls.","command":{"name":"get_classes_and_methods","args":{"project_name":"oci","bug_index":1,"file_path":"src/libcrun/container.c"}}}{"thoughts":"The symbol listing is sparse, but the previously read range shows the failing `execvp` at line 652. I still need the immediately preceding setup code from the container init function to confirm whether `process.env` is installed before exec and whether replacing `execvp` with `execvpe` (or equivalent PATH lookup against OCI env) is sufficient. The next focused read should cover the omitted lines 400-660 around signal handling, namespace/container setup, env setup, and final exec.","command":{"name":"read_range","args":{"project_name":"oci","bug_index":1,"filepath":"src/libcrun/container.c","startline":400,"endline":660}}}{"thoughts":"The previous read was truncated before the most relevant section. I need a smaller focused range from after pivot_root through the final exec to see exactly where environment variables are applied and to design a minimal PATH lookup fix without broad inspection.","command":{"name":"read_range","args":{"project_name":"oci","bug_index":1,"filepath":"src/libcrun/container.c","startline":500,"endline":660}}}{"thoughts":"The focused range confirms environment is cleared and the OCI process env is installed before returning from container_entrypoint_init. The remaining needed evidence is the exact exec call just after the truncated part; a very small range will capture it and enable a line-oriented fix.","command":{"name":"read_range","args":{"project_name":"oci","bug_index":1,"filepath":"src/libcrun/container.c","startline":590,"endline":657}}}{"thoughts":"The evidence pinpoints the bare execvp call. Since the OCI process environment has already been installed, a simple robust fix is to resolve argv[0] explicitly against the container's PATH and then execv the resolved path, avoiding libc execvp's implicit lookup behavior. I will inspect utilities for an existing PATH lookup helper before editing, to keep the patch small and consistent.","command":{"name":"search_code_base","args":{"project_name":"oci","bug_index":1,"key_words":"PATH execv execvp find executable"}}}{"thoughts":"The broad search was noisy, but the focused evidence shows the launch site at src/libcrun/container.c:652. To avoid relying on implicit execvp PATH handling at the final exec point, I will add explicit PATH resolution just before exec. This keeps the process environment from OCI config as the source of PATH, preserves absolute/relative paths containing '/', and then uses execv on the resolved pathname. A comment will be inserted above the altered code as required, and write_fix will build the candidate.","command":{"name":"write_fix","args":{"project_name":"oci","bug_index":1,"changes_dicts":[{"file_name":"src/libcrun/container.c","insertions":[{"line_number":651,"new_lines":["","  /* Resolve a bare process name with the container's PATH before exec.","     execvp() performs this lookup implicitly at exec time; doing it here makes","     the lookup use the OCI process environment that was just installed and","     passes an explicit container pathname to execv().  */","  if (strchr (def->process->args[0], '/') == NULL)","    {","      const char *path = getenv (\"PATH\");","      char *paths = NULL;","      char *saveptr = NULL;","      char *dir;","","      if (path == NULL || path[0] == '\\0')","        path = \"/bin:/usr/bin\";","","      paths = xstrdup (path);","      for (dir = strtok_r (paths, \":\", &saveptr); dir; dir = strtok_r (NULL, \":\", &saveptr))","        {","          cleanup_free char *candidate = NULL;","","          if (dir[0] == '\\0')","            dir = \".\";","","          xasprintf (&candidate, \"%s/%s\", dir, def->process->args[0]);","          if (access (candidate, X_OK) == 0)","            {","              execv (candidate, def->process->args);","              break;","            }","        }","      free (paths);","    }"]}],"deletions":[],"modifications":[{"line_number":652,"modified_line":"  execv (def->process->args[0], def->process->args);"}]}]}}}